{"type":"after","callId":"gfsl@1213","endTime":157703.917,"result":{"value":"All projects\nWEB EXPERIENCE / 01\nLivSocial.\n\nA social web experience bringing posts, communities, business discovery, and personal connections into one workspace.\n\nPROJECT TYPE\nWeb & web apps\nFOCUS\nSocial & community\nPROJECT ARTWORK\nOverview\nKey features\nHow it works\nSolution\nDesign\nTechnical\nScreenshots\nDevice views\n01\nPROJECT OVERVIEW\nA place for conversations to grow.\n\nLivSocial’s desktop artwork presents a central content feed alongside a personal social circle and trending conversations. Navigation separates the home feed, communities, businesses, and profile areas. The result is a view of a social product organized around both people and the content they share.\n\n02\nKEY FEATURES\nDesigned around\nthe experience.\n\nA social workspace where the main feed, personal connections, and wider community discovery each have a clear place.\n\nContent feed\n\nImage posts and written updates sit together in the main reading column.\n\nCommunity navigation\n\nDedicated entry points distinguish communities, businesses, and personal areas.\n\nLivSocial / Original interface\nSocial circle\n\nA side panel brings people and their profiles into view.\n\nTrending conversations\n\nSupporting content helps visitors discover subjects beyond their own feed.\n\n03\nPRODUCT JOURNEY\nHow LivSocial works.\n\nThe desktop layouts move from an everyday feed to the people and conversations around it.\n\n01\nStart with the feed\n\nRead photo posts and written updates in the central column, with familiar post controls close to the content.\n\n02\nExplore a community\n\nUse the main navigation to move into communities or businesses without losing the recognizable social frame.\n\n03\nFollow the conversation\n\nOpen profile and topic areas to explore the people and discussions surrounding an individual post.\n\n04\nDESIGN CHALLENGE & SOLUTION\nMake a busy community feel connected.\n\nSocial products need to show more than a stream of posts. LivSocial's layout gives people, topics, and community areas their own positions around a consistent reading space.\n\nA clear reading column\n\nThe central feed has priority, while secondary discovery remains in supporting side panels.\n\nPeople in context\n\nAvatars and social-circle information keep personal connections visible beside the shared content.\n\nRecognizable destinations\n\nNamed navigation areas separate the home feed, communities, businesses, and personal spaces.\n\nLivSocial / Design detail\n05\nDESIGN DIRECTION\nIts own identity.\nIn every detail.\nSocial & community\n\nMustard yellow establishes the product identity, while white content panels keep photo posts and conversations readable. A persistent desktop navigation bar and supporting side columns give the main feed a clear position within a much broader community experience.\n\nDesign observations from the supplied project artwork.\n06\nTECHNICAL PERSPECTIVE\nA layered information architecture.\n\nPosts, profiles, communities, and trending subjects appear as distinct content types. Repeated card treatments connect those surfaces visually, while persistent navigation makes their relationship understandable across the supplied desktop screens.\n\nFeed hierarchy\nProfile surfaces\nCommunity navigation\nCLARIGO ENGINEERING TOOLKIT\nReact\nNext.js\nNode.js\nFlutter\nPython\nDocker\n\nPublished company capabilities. The original project material does not identify a project-specific technology stack.\n\nExplore Clarigo's app development\n07\nUI SCREENSHOTS & ARTWORK\nInside LivSocial.\n\nExplore the original interface screens. Select any image for a closer look.\n\nINTERFACE SCREEN\n01\nINTERFACE SCREEN\n02\nINTERFACE SCREEN\n03\nINTERFACE SCREEN\n04\nINTERFACE SCREEN\n05\n08\nRESPONSIVE DESIGN PRESENTATION\nA view across\nthe original devices.\n\nLivSocial's original portfolio artwork presents the product in its supplied device composition. This presentation retains those source layouts and their original proportions.\n\nOriginal project mockups, rather than newly generated screenshots of a live product.\n\nLivSocial / Original device composition\nSOURCE MATERIAL\n\nDescriptions, journeys, and design considerations interpret the artwork and available overview. They do not imply unpublished client briefs, verified implementation details, app-store availability, or measured business results.\n\nOriginal project page\nNEXT WEB PROJECT\nStreamDexa\nKEEP EXPLORING\nMore perspectives.\nView all work\nDIGITAL ASSETS & DISCOVERY\nStreamDexa\nCHILDCARE & FAMILY\nLittle Butterflies\nORGANIZATION & COLLABORATION\nTukioConnect\nYOUR NEXT PRODUCT\nInspired by\nLivSocial?\n\nPlanning a community platform? Let's shape the people, content, and discovery experience around your audience.\n\nDiscuss your project\nExplore the mobile project\nBrowse all 47 projects"}}
